  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:81406",
  "description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: thermal: core: Fix thermal zone device registration error path (CVE-2026-43332)\n  * kernel: macsec: fix replay protection at XPN lower-PN wrap (CVE-2026-63925)\n  * kernel: i2c: stub: Reject I2C block transfers with invalid length (CVE-2026-64191)\n  * kernel: Kernel SMB client: Double-free vulnerability allows remote denial of service or privilege escalation (CVE-2026-64385)\n  * kernel: bpf: Support for hardening against JIT spraying (CVE-2026-64508)\n  * kernel: x86/bugs: Enable IBPB flush on BPF JIT allocation (CVE-2026-64507)\n  * kernel: openvswitch: fix GSO userspace truncation underflow (CVE-2026-68123)\n  * kernel: cifs: validate DFS referral string offsets (CVE-2026-72318)\n  * kernel: KVM: arm64: vgic: Check the interrupt is still ours before migrating it (CVE-2026-72289)\n  * kernel: af_unix: Unlink scc_entry in unix_del_edge() (CVE-2026-80521)\n  * kernel: nvmet-auth: Synchronize timeout work during SQ teardown (CVE-2026-89970)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * net/tls backports for 10.2 (JIRA:AlmaLinux-275027)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
